---
import { themes } from "@wonder-wagon/themes";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="Products" description="Who uses Wonder Wagon UI and what each product consumes.">
  <div class="stack"><span class="plate muted">Products</span><h1>Four tools, one bench</h1><p class="muted prose">Siblings, never identical. Each keeps its own hero object, its own adapter and its own class names; the family is the metal, the light and Maker 047.</p></div>
  <section class="grid-2">
    <div class="card" id="pathfinder"><span class="tag">Pathfinder · PF-047 · approved</span><h2 style="font-size:var(--ww-text-3)">The compatibility proof</h2><p style="font-size:var(--ww-text-0)">Pathfinder shipped a hand-written <code>--ww-*</code> semantic block in its Starlight adapter. <code>@wonder-wagon/themes/adapters/pathfinder</code> regenerates it from tokens and the Pathfinder theme; the proof holds all 34 declarations, day and night, to the shipped values at a pinned commit. Its atlascope, four-bar mark and renderer stay Pathfinder's.</p><span class="stamp">34 / 34 reproduced</span></div>
    <div class="card" id="forge"><span class="tag">Forge · FG-047 · pilot</span><h2 style="font-size:var(--ww-text-3)">The React-free proof</h2><p style="font-size:var(--ww-text-0)">Forge is a Node CLI with zero production dependencies and a byte-verified tarball. It takes <code>@wonder-wagon/themes</code> as a devDependency, regenerates a committed <code>identity.ts</code> — bronze in three terminal alphabets, severity left to the terminal's own colours — and checks it for drift in CI. No React enters its graph.</p><span class="stamp">No React · deterministic</span></div>
    <div class="card"><span class="tag">Lorekeeper · LK-047 · draft</span><h2 style="font-size:var(--ww-text-3)">Absorbed, not redesigned</h2><p style="font-size:var(--ww-text-0)">Indigo, gilt, parchment and the four-point star survive from its shipped identity. Its own <code>tokens.json → build.mjs --check</code> pipeline is the pattern this system generalised; the theme is a draft until its pilot.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><span class="tag">Lama · LM-047 · draft</span><h2 style="font-size:var(--ww-text-3)">The React consumer, later</h2><p style="font-size:var(--ww-text-0)">The one application in the family, on Next.js. It becomes the first production consumer of <code>@wonder-wagon/ui</code> after Forge proves the framework-independent foundation.</p></div>
  </section>
  <section class="stack"><div class="section-plate"><h2>Serials</h2><span class="rule"></span></div>
    <div class="row">{Object.values(themes).map((t) => <span class="chip"><i style={`background:${t.enamel.day}`}></i>{t.serial}-047 · {t.name}</span>)}</div>
    <p class="muted prose" style="font-size:var(--ww-text-0)">047 is the maker; the whole family came from one bench. The prefix says which thing this is.</p></section>
</Base>
